#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "There are two support collection methods, the first utilizes the legacy flow-tools binaries and the second leverages Cacti's own PHP based flow stream server."
msgstr "Hari uburyo bubiri bwemewe bwo gukusanya amakuru, ubwa mbere bukoresha porogaramu za kera za flow-tools naho ubwa kabiri bukifashisha seriveri y'umuyoboro wa flow ya Cacti ubwayo ishingiye kuri PHP."

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "Bind to address"
msgstr "Huza na aderesi"

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "If Cacti server has more IP Addresses, you can specify specific interface. Leave as 0.0.0.0 for primary interface."
msgstr "Niba seriveri ya Cacti ifite Aderesi za IP nyinshi, ushobora kwerekana interefasi yihariye. Reka bibe 0.0.0.0 kuri interefasi y'ibanze."

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "Allowed Host Range"
msgstr "Igice cya Mwakirizi cyemewe"

#: flowview_devices.php
msgid "IP Address of the device that is allowed to send to this flow collector.  Leave as 0.0.0.0 for any host.  Note that PHP is finicky about what it allows.  CIDR syntax is supported as well as range syntax for example 192.168.1.0 or 192.168.1.0/24.  If you want specific IP addresses, separate them by a comma."
msgstr "Aderesi ya IP y'igikoresho cyemerewe kohereza kuri uyu mukusanyiriza w'imigendekere (flow collector).  Reka bibe 0.0.0.0 kuri mwakirizi uwo ari we wese.  Menya ko PHP igorana ku byo yemera.  Imyandikire ya CIDR iremewe kimwe n'imyandikire y'intera urugero 192.168.1.0 cyangwa 192.168.1.0/24.  Niba ushaka aderesi za IP zihariye, zitandukanye ukoresheje akitso."

